# A problem

Import UiProfile from "../src/ui_profile.lg".
Import UiResults from "../src/ui_results.lg".
Import UiSite from "../src/ui_site.lg".
Import UiStatements from "../src/ui_statements.lg".
Import UiTrail from "../src/ui_trail.lg".
Import WebProblem from "../src/web_problem.lg".

One problem's page, `/problem?id=<problem id>`: the problem and its OPDP profile,
its formal statements, every attempt on its trail with what the kernel said, the
lemma tree below it, and the verdicts the trusted verifier signed. The id travels
in the query because problem ids may hold slashes; a visitor may also paste one
into the form. Each section fetches its own list when it appears.

## Page /problem

Head:
    <title>MaCSad — a problem</title>

State:
    Let id be "".
    Let draft be "".
    Let problem be a new ProblemView.
    Let found be false.
    Let error be "".

Actions:
    To open (pid: Text):
        If trim(pid) is equal to "":
            Return.
        Set id to trim(pid).
        Set found to false.
        Set error to "".
        Get "/api/v1/problem?id=" + urlEncode(id) as ProblemView, then arrived.

    When the page loads:
        Call open with routeQuery("id").

    To submitId:
        Call open with draft.

    To arrived (answer: Result of ProblemView and HttpError):
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (p):
                Set problem to p.
                Set found to true.
                Set the title to "MaCSad — " + p's title.
            When Err (e):
                Set error to e's message.

View:
    {extends Site}
    {block content:}
      <form class="form-row" id="open-form" on-submit.prevent={submitId}>
        <label>Problem id<input id="problem-id" bind={draft} placeholder="opdp:116, op:OP022, fc:ErdosProblems/10"></label>
        <button class="primary" type="submit">Open</button>
      </form>
      {if error is not equal to "":}<p class="error-banner" role="alert" id="error">{error}</p>{end}
      {if found:}
        <ProblemHead p={problem}/>
        <div class="grid-2">
          <div class="stack"><ProblemProfile p={problem}/><StatementSection pid={id}/><TrailSection pid={id} check={problem's trailCheck}/></div>
          <div class="stack"><ResultSection pid={id}/><LemmaSection pid={id}/></div>
        </div>
      {else:}
        <p class="empty" id="pick">Open a problem from the <a href="/">atlas</a>, or paste its id above.</p>
      {end}
    {end}

## Test: a problem opens with its profile and an empty trail

Given that GET "/api/v1/problem?id=opdp%3A116" answers 200 with """{{"id": "opdp:116", "title": "Gowers box norms", "status": "open",
  "stage": "ranked", "rankBp": 6100, "source": "opdp", "cohort": "UnsolvedMath", "collection": "green-problems", "category": "combinatorics",
  "statementInformal": "Let p be an odd prime.", "leanStatement": "", "leanModule": "", "leanDeclaration": "", "externalKey": "GREEN-1",
  "crossRef": "", "difficultyLabel": "T4 Hard", "difficulty": "7.9", "tier": "T4", "aiFit": "AI-favorable", "aiDifficulty": "6.1",
  "tractability": "T3", "progress": "10-20%", "formalization": "3.1", "verification": "4.0", "toolLeverage": "5.5",
  "route": "Literature audit", "effortHours": "300-1,000", "explanation": "A serious project.", "attempts": 2, "claimed": 0,
  "attested": 0, "spentMicros": 1250, "trailLength": 2, "deadEnds": 1, "openUnits": 1, "trailCheck": "intact"}}""".
Given that GET "/api/v1/problem/timeline?id=opdp%3A116&limit=200" answers 200 with "[]".
Given that GET "/api/v1/problem/statements?id=opdp%3A116" answers 200 with "[]".
Type "opdp:116" into "#problem-id".
Submit "#open-form".
Expect that the text of "#problem-title" is equal to "Gowers box norms".
Expect that the text of "#attempts" is equal to "2".
Expect that the count of "#opdp div" is equal to 10.
Expect that the text of "#trail-check" is equal to "chain intact".
Expect that the text of "#no-statements" is equal to "No formal statement yet: the problem is waiting for a formalize unit.".

## Test: an unknown problem says so and draws nothing

Given that GET "/api/v1/problem?id=nope" answers 404 with "problem nope is not known to the coordinator".
Type "nope" into "#problem-id".
Submit "#open-form".
Expect that the text of "#error" is equal to "404: problem nope is not known to the coordinator".
Expect that "#problem-title" is hidden.
